Toolbay Stack
=============

Toolbay Stack is built on gstack by Garry Tan.

    gstack
    https://github.com/garrytan/gstack
    Copyright (c) 2026 Garry Tan
    Licensed under the MIT License

gstack is the origin of this project's core idea and of a substantial part of
its workflow skills: the persistent browser daemon, the skill-per-directory
layout, the multi-host distribution model, and the review/ship/QA workflow
family. Where Toolbay Stack forks a gstack skill, the derived file carries an
attribution header naming gstack and Garry Tan, and the MIT notice above is
reproduced in full in the LICENSE file at the root of this repository.

Toolbay Stack is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Garry Tan.
Please do not report Toolbay Stack issues to the gstack project.

If you want the original, use the original. It is excellent and it is upstream:

    https://github.com/garrytan/gstack


New work in this repository
---------------------------

Everything under the following paths is original to Toolbay Stack and is
Copyright (c) 2026 Toolbay, MIT licensed:

    bin/                 the installer CLI
    src/cursor/          the Cursor integration and hook adapter
    tools/               build tooling
    skills/toolbay/      the marketplace connector skill
    skills/router/       the skill-routing layer
    skills/modes/        the stance layer (modes)
    skills/suggest/      the project-state suggestion engine
    skills/memory/       the correction-recall layer
    skills/video/        the prompt-to-video layer
    skills/backtest/     the setup-backtest harness
    docs/

skills/modes/, skills/suggest/, skills/memory/ and skills/backtest/ have no
counterpart in gstack. They ship inside gstack's skill-per-directory layout and
they change how the forked skills are reached and how they behave once reached,
but no code or contract in any of the four is derived from gstack.
skills/suggest/ names commands by importing skills/router/, and never by a table
of its own.

skills/backtest/ measures a user's own agent configuration against seeded
defects. It reads and executes whatever hooks that user has configured, which on
some machines will be gstack's; it never writes inside gstack's skill directory
and contains no gstack code.

src/cursor/ installs this stack into Cursor (https://cursor.com), a separate
product by Anysphere which is NOT bundled, vendored or redistributed here: the
installer locates an installation on the machine and refuses when there is none.
gstack has no Cursor integration, so nothing in it is derived from gstack. The
Cursor hook format it writes is Cursor's own, documented by Anysphere.

skills/video/ is original work with no counterpart in gstack. It drives
Diffusion Studio's `dapi` command line tool
(https://github.com/diffusionstudio/editor, MIT), which is a separate project
and is NOT bundled, vendored or redistributed here: the skill locates an
installation on the machine and refuses when there is none. No Diffusion Studio
code is included in this repository.

skills/modes/ is the one that reaches furthest into the forked skills: a mode is
a stance that a forked SKILL.md reads and follows at the top of its run, so the
same gstack-derived workflow produces a different amount of work in a different
mode. The stance layer is ours. Every workflow it modulates is still credited to
gstack in that skill's own header.


