Why the explanation lives here and not in LICENSE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LICENSE contains the MIT grant and nothing else, verbatim. An earlier version
explained this derivation inside that file, and GitHub reported the project as
NOASSERTION — legally MIT, machine-readably nothing, so no scanner, package
index or corporate policy tool could confirm what it is. Automated license
detectors match the grant text closely and are thrown by prose around it.

So the grant stays clean and every word of explanation lives in this file,
which is what a NOTICE file is for. Nothing about the attribution is reduced by
the move; it is more findable here, next to the file-by-file record.
